    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "A useful mental model for the creational patterns is a restaurant kitchen. A Factory Method is a station chef who knows how to prepare one dish and hands it off when asked, without the front-of-house staff needing to know the recipe. An Abstract Factory is closer to an entire themed menu - Italian night or Japanese night - where every dish produced that evening is guaranteed to belong to the same coherent set. Builder is the multi-course tasting menu assembled step by step, where the order of courses and their combination matters more than any single dish. Singleton is the one head chef in the kitchen - there's only one, and every station defers to that single point of authority whether or not that's actually a good idea for the restaurant's scalability."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
